  ],
  "title": "*Atuna",
  "provenance": "Pleiades",
  "placeTypeURIs": [
    "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/place-types/unlocated",
    "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/place-types/settlement"
  ],
  "details": "<p>The city is mentioned in royal inscriptions of the Assyrian kings Tiglath-pileser III (r. 744-727 BC) and Sargon II (r. 721-705). Two locations have been suggested for the city *Atuna: (1)\u00a0in the vicinity of Boz\u00e7a (Boh<span>\u00e7a)</span>, on the K\u0131z\u0131l\u0131rmak river, ca. 40 km west of Kayseri; and (2) in the vicinity of Porsuk/Zeyve H\u00fcy\u00fck. The latter is based on the proposed location of\u00a0classical Tynna, a city that might be identified with *Atuna. For further details, see the Place Resource for\u00a0T<a class=\"external-link\" href=\"../648802\" target=\"_self\" title=\"\">ynna/Dana?</a>.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "*Atuna is the capital of the kingdom *Atuna in Tabal.",
